[DOCUMENT]
MID: 2f0e50acf0384cebb452af661ea7b29d
TITLE: System requirements
UID: DOC-SYS
OPTIONS:
  ENABLE_MID: True
  VIEW_STYLE: Table

[[SECTION]]
MID: bfc8f19603e348f8a2ace6b1c976f27c
TITLE: Purpose

[TEXT]
MID: 84add85cf52f4df7bef729b66e57add5
STATEMENT: >>>
This document states what the motor control system must do, as seen by the
operator and by the team that ports the firmware to a new board. The software
requirements in ``software_requirements.sdoc`` refine each item here.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
MID: 5ea88dfe403d403c85349a0d413dd5ef
TITLE: Motor control

[REQUIREMENT]
MID: 72612bdc4b074e2ebf79f2e61af0e0c0
UID: SYS-001
TITLE: Closed-loop speed control
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall hold the motor shaft speed within 2 % of the commanded
setpoint in steady state, and shall settle to that band within 1 s of a start
command.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The driven load needs a known speed. Open-loop duty control drifts with supply
voltage and load torque.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
MID: a2571fb580dd4c3a9e9830f16e69ba24
UID: SYS-002
TITLE: Operator start and stop
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall start the motor when the operator presses the start button,
and shall stop the motor when the operator presses the stop button.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
MID: 2f124adc09f4491f8428e35fe40394f5
TITLE: Protection

[REQUIREMENT]
MID: dd4900bdff124287a894708a193b850c
UID: SYS-003
TITLE: Overcurrent protection
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall disable the motor drive within one control period when the
motor current exceeds the configured limit.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Sustained overcurrent damages the H-bridge and the motor windings.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
MID: 94076d7587ce4a81a8b7daceccd7b2fd
UID: SYS-004
TITLE: Stall protection
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall disable the motor drive when the motor is driven but does not
turn for a configured time.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
MID: 456c178005dc407981f6c92d8a7642ba
UID: SYS-005
TITLE: Fault recovery
STATEMENT: >>>
After a fault, the system shall keep the drive disabled until the operator
presses the stop button to acknowledge the fault.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
MID: b691a37cfeb8426988b96ac8d332f7e8
TITLE: Quality attributes

[REQUIREMENT]
MID: cd51b4299f244392ab032c263b73ab8f
UID: SYS-006
TITLE: Platform portability
STATEMENT: >>>
The application and domain logic shall build without change for any MCU that
provides an implementation of the HAL interfaces in ``src/hal``.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The product line uses more than one MCU vendor. A port must only touch the HAL
port and the board support package.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
MID: 99846ceb5c3d489cadb9547469c2f2fb
UID: SYS-007
TITLE: Deterministic behavior
STATEMENT: >>>
The control loop shall run at a fixed period of 1 ms, and shall produce the
same outputs for the same inputs on every target.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Floating-point rounding, heap allocation and unbounded loops make timing and
results differ between targets and between runs.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
MID: 5e7d6db74d9346d095080bdc9912fd75
UID: SYS-008
TITLE: Host testability
STATEMENT: >>>
All logic above the HAL port shall be testable on a development host without
target hardware.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]
